    "rich_text_hJa8hj": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_E3pdTr": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "How to Choose the Right Smartwatch for Women",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "heading_width": 600
          }
        },
        "text_UHcncP": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>When shopping for a women's smartwatch, start with the features and fit that matter most to your routine.</p><p><strong>Check the wrist size.</strong> A smaller case doesn't always mean a better fit. Compare your wrist circumference with the manufacturer's published band range.</p><p><strong>Consider your daily activities.</strong> If you exercise frequently, a silicone band may be more convenient. If you prefer classic everyday styling, leather could be a better match.</p><p><strong>Review smartphone compatibility.</strong> Confirm that the watch and companion app work with your phone and support the notifications you need.</p><p><strong>Look at the wellness features.</strong> Choose tracking functions you'll actually use, such as daily activity, heart rate, or sleep monitoring.</p><p><strong>Think about personalization.</strong> Interchangeable bands and customizable watch faces can make a smartwatch suitable for different occasions.</p><p>For more help choosing the right size, read our <a href=\"https://fany.us/blogs/wellness-fitness/best-smartwatch-for-small-wrists\">Smartwatch Guide for Small Wrists</a>.</p>",
            "font_size": "f-18",
            "text_width": 800
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_E3pdTr",
        "text_UHcncP"
